\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Blocked-set prediction on a disjoint-window geometry (experiment 10). The geometric kernel beats both empirical kernels at every deletion depth --- it is noise-free and structurally consistent where empirical estimates carry sampling noise --- and the zero-trajectory model beats winner-only \emph  {trajectory} models on pair and triple blocks. Note the two-kernels warning realized: all-pairs estimation is strictly worse than first-transitions.}}{6}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:exp10}{{2}{6}{Blocked-set prediction on a disjoint-window geometry (experiment 10). The geometric kernel beats both empirical kernels at every deletion depth --- it is noise-free and structurally consistent where empirical estimates carry sampling noise --- and the zero-trajectory model beats winner-only \emph {trajectory} models on pair and triple blocks. Note the two-kernels warning realized: all-pairs estimation is strictly worse than first-transitions}{table.2}{}}
